# Enigma Drake (*/4 flying): "Enigma Drake's power is equal to the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard" - a
# characteristic-defining ability (CR 604.3, layer 7a). Bot1 casts it on turn 1 off Black Lotus and a Mountain: the Lotus lands in the
# graveyard, but an artifact is not an instant or sorcery, so the Drake is 0/4. Bot2's Lightning Bolt in turn 2 hits the Drake for 3
# (it survives, toughness 4) and goes to Bot2's graveyard, which is not Bot1's, so the power stays 0. On turn 3 Bot1 bolts its own
# Memnite: the graveyard holds an artifact, a creature and one instant, so the power is 1. On turn 5 Chain Lightning (a sorcery)
# makes it 2, and the Drake attacks for exactly that.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Enigma Drake
Memnite
Lightning Bolt
Chain Lightning
Island
Mountain
Mountain
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
